      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Long-term oral treatment of patients with acute coronary syndromes and type 2 diabetes mellitus with beta-adrenoblockers and angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors is associated with positive, though ambiguous changes in the left-ventricular structure and function. These changes should be the reason for choosing optimal therapy ensuring better prognosis in this patient population."},
